GPU cycles per submission (real core clock) and a DDR (BIMC) vote (spesddr_khz).

all40 (0162) measured the GPU itself: 60-130 ms per UI submission (29-35 per 5 s while in use, about
60 ms even for an idle redraw), so the Metal UI is GPU-bound at 8-12 fps; CPU-side cache push is
~1 ms. That is far more than a compositor frame should take at 300 MHz. Two suspects:
- the clock: 0107 selects GPLL0/2 but never measured it. RBBM_PERFCTR_RBBM_0 (countable 0,
  ALWAYS_COUNT, enabled with RBBM_PERFCTR_CNTL = 1 as msm a6xx_hw_init) is now stamped next to
  CP_ALWAYS_ON_COUNTER; "SPES GPU: core clock measured N MHz" each stats period.
- memory bandwidth: nothing ever voted the BIMC. Live FDT: fab-bimc bus_clk is an RPM clock; kgsl's
  grp3d table pairs 320 MHz with 4.4 GB/s and 1115 MHz with 16.7 GB/s. spesddr_khz=N sends RPM
  "clk2"/0 "KHz"=N on the active set over the GPU probe's link (spes_rpm_kvp); 0 = no vote.

